  "stem": "A line in the \\(xy\\)-plane has a slope of \\(-\\frac{1}{2}\\) and passes through the points \\((3, a)\\) and \\((7, 2)\\). What is the value of \\(a\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "4"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "\\(\\frac{2 - a}{7 - 3} = -\\frac{1}{2}\\), so \\(2 - a = -2\\).",
    "So \\(a = 4\\)."
  ],
  "verify": "a = symbols('a')\nsol = solve(Eq((2 - a)/(7 - 3), Rational(-1, 2)), a)\nassert sol == [4]\nassert [Rational(s) for s in spr_answers] == sol",
